//@version=6
indicator("EzyMap Pro V1.9", shorttitle="EzyMap Pro", overlay=true, max_bars_back=5000, max_lines_count=30, max_boxes_count=20, max_labels_count=180, dynamic_requests=true)

//==================================================================================================
// EZYMAP PRO V1.9
// Carries forward everything from V1.8 with one addition: a fair value gap
// (FVG) fill is now a fifth, independent confirmation type, alongside
// rejection wick, liquidity sweep+reclaim, session/premium sweep+reclaim,
// displacement CHOCH and plain structure-break CHOCH.
//
// An FVG is the classic 3-candle imbalance: on the routed entry timeframe,
// if the oldest of three consecutive candles doesn't overlap the price
// range of the newest at all, the untraded gap between them is the FVG.
// Each of the four zones (BUY-HIGH/BUY-LOW/SELL-HIGH/SELL-LOW) tracks the
// most recent bullish/bearish FVG independently and treats it as a valid
// confirmation once that gap overlaps the zone itself — the FVG sitting
// right where the S/R zone is means a return into the zone is also a
// return into unfilled imbalance, same idea as sweep/displacement already
// being scored only when their event candle overlaps the zone. Recency
// uses the same 4-entry-candle ARMED_CONFIRMATION_WINDOW as every other
// confirmation type. FVG also adds +1 to confluence scoring (in line with
// EMA slope/regime/VWAP; lighter than MTF cluster or displacement's +2)
// and appears in the trade card's extra-reasons list as "FAIR VALUE GAP
// FILL". A CHOCH that coincides with an FVG at the same zone is now
// attributed to the FVG in the reasons list (not double-counted as a bare
// CHOCH), the same way it was already deferred to displacement.
//
// Carries forward from V1.8, unchanged — one structural change:
//
// HIGH RISK (S1/R1) and LOW RISK (S2/R2) zones are now independent
// live-signal triggers per direction, instead of every route (trend and
// counter-trend alike) arming only the LOW RISK zone. There are now four
// independent armed slots — BUY-HIGH, BUY-LOW, SELL-HIGH, SELL-LOW — each
// with its own confirmation/confluence/MTF/VWAP evaluation keyed to its
// own zone coordinates and S1/S2/R1/R2 level. CHOCH (structure-break)
// confirmation applies identically in both zones per direction, exactly
// as it already did before this change, since CHOCH was never tied to a
// specific S/R level. All four slots can be independently READY at the
// same time; the moment any one of them fires, the existing single
// ACTIVE-trade lock (now keyed only on direction, not risk tier) still
// allows just one ACTIVE trade per direction at a time, same as before.
// The dynamic zone box styling was updated to match — all four boxes
// (BUY-HIGH, BUY-LOW, SELL-HIGH, SELL-LOW) can now independently show
// READY, and LIVE is decided by which risk tier the current ACTIVE trade
// actually came from.
//
// Superseded text from V1.7, kept for history:
// 1) "Minimum Confluence for LIVE Trigger" reverted back to a default of
//    0 (undoing V1.6's change to 2) — still a fully adjustable input.
// 2) Both trend-following and counter-trend routes now arm on the LOW
//    RISK zone (S2 for BUY, R2 for SELL) instead of trend-following using
//    the near HIGH RISK zone (S1/R1) as before — a deeper, more
//    significant level for the live-signal trigger specifically. The
//    HIGH RISK boxes still draw on the map for reference; only the zone
//    actually armed/traded moved, so the dynamic READY/LIVE box
//    restyling was updated to match — only the LOW box can highlight now,
//    the HIGH box stays plain map styling.
//
// Superseded text from V1.6, kept for history:
// 1) "Minimum Confluence for LIVE Trigger" default raised from 0 to 2.
//    It's an existing input (unchanged since V1.1's marker-comparison
//    test) that had been left at 0 ever since, meaning it gated nothing —
//    every touch went LIVE regardless of supporting evidence. Confluence
//    always starts at a base count of 1 (the S&R level itself), so
//    requiring 2 filters out the bare setups with zero corroborating
//    factors (no round number, no EMA/trendline/Fib proximity, no MTF
//    agreement, no sweep/premium/displacement, no EMA slope/regime, no
//    VWAP). Since sweep, premium-sweep and displacement confirmations
//    also score confluence bonus points, this indirectly filters out the
//    weakest confirmation type too — a plain structure-break CHOCH with
//    nothing else backing it, the most common and least selective of the
//    four confirmation paths, is exactly the kind of setup this raises
//    the bar on without singling CHOCH out by name. Still a fully
//    adjustable input; set it back to 0 to compare against V1.5 if the
//    frequency/quality trade-off doesn't land right.
//
// Carries forward from V1.5, unchanged:
//
// 1) A genuinely-alerted ACTIVE trade could vanish from the dashboard
//    without ever hitting TP, SL or BE — the historical-to-realtime
//    boundary reset unconditionally wiped all trade state, and that
//    boundary re-fires on any silent data-feed reconnect (e.g. a
//    backgrounded browser tab), not just a fresh script load. Now it only
//    clears the ACTIVE trade fields when state isn't already "ACTIVE";
//    READY zones are still always cleared there since they never alerted.
// 2) The permanent BUY/SELL marker used to be created only inside the
//    one-shot alert-commit tick, gated by enableAlerts/alertLive — a
//    missed tick or disabled alerts meant no marker, ever, even for a
//    trade that genuinely alerted. It now runs every bar a trade is
//    ACTIVE, independent of the alert path.
// 3) The trade card's post-result display window was a hardcoded 10
//    seconds — long enough to vanish before switching from a phone push
//    notification back to the chart. It's now an adjustable input
//    ("Result Visible Seconds", Display group), default 30.
// 4) The confirmation-name lookup had no branch for a plain
//    structure-break CHOCH (added as a standalone confirmation path
//    in V1.2) — it fell through to an empty string whenever CHOCH was
//    the only confirmation reason, showing blank on the trade card's
//    "WHY THIS TRADE" line. Added "STRUCTURE BREAK (CHOCH)" as the
//    fallback branch.
//
// 5) Requested zone refinement: each S1/S2/R1/R2 zone is now the
//    rejection wick only, not the full candle range or V1.4's
//    multi-candle extreme-widening. For the single candle nearest to CMP
//    that overlaps a level: a support/BUY zone is low-to-close (the wick
//    below where price settled), and a resistance/SELL zone is
//    close-to-high (the wick above where price settled) — sharper,
//    tighter entries anchored to where price actually got rejected. A
//    minimum height (10 mintick) guards against a candle that closed
//    exactly at its high or low producing a zero-height zone. Requires
//    the support-timeframe candle bank to also carry close prices
//    (previously only high/low/time), so f_support_bank() and the
//    supportCloses request.security/array wiring were added alongside it.
//==================================================================================================

//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inputs
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
const string G1="01 • Engine"
const string G2="02 • Confirmation"
const string G3="03 • Risk"
const string G4="04 • Display"
const string G5="05 • Alerts"
const string G6="06 • Premium Theme"
const string G8="07 • Trade Management"

string chartTfSelection=input.string("AUTO","Chart Timeframe",options=["AUTO","1","5","15","30","60","240"],group=G1,display=display.none)
const int directionEmaLength=13
int supportPivotBars=input.int(3,"Supporting Swing Bars",minval=2,maxval=8,group=G1,display=display.none)
float levelDistinctPips=input.float(10.0,"Minimum Level Separation",minval=1.0,maxval=100.0,step=1.0,group=G1,display=display.none)

int entryPivotBars=input.int(1,"Entry CHoCH Swing Bars",minval=1,maxval=5,group=G2,display=display.none)
bool requireDirectionalBody=input.bool(false,"Require Directional Confirmation Body",group=G2,display=display.none)
float rejectionWickRatio=input.float(0.25,"Rejection Wick / Body Ratio",minval=0.20,maxval=3.0,step=0.05,group=G2,display=display.none)
// Pro V1.1: confluence count is a visible, adjustable LIVE-trigger threshold
// instead of a hardcoded gate. Confluence always starts at 1 (the base S&R
// level itself), so 0 never blocks anything — this reproduces V1's tested
// "no confluence gate" behavior exactly at the default. Raise it to require
// more evidence before LIVE releases, and compare the historical BUY/SELL
// marker positions between settings. It is calculated and shown on the trade
// card as CONFIDENCE regardless of what this threshold is set to.
int minimumConfluenceForLive=input.int(0,"Minimum Confluence for LIVE Trigger",minval=0,maxval=10,group=G2,display=display.none)
int armedExpiryEntryBars=input.int(60,"READY Expiry (Entry bars)",minval=3,maxval=60,group=G2,display=display.none)
float confluenceTolerancePips=input.float(70.0,"Confluence Tolerance",minval=5.0,maxval=200.0,step=5.0,group=G2,display=display.none)
bool useMtfLevelCluster=input.bool(true,"Use Multi-Timeframe Level Cluster",group=G2,display=display.none)
bool useSweepReclaim=input.bool(true,"Use Completed Liquidity Sweep + Reclaim",group=G2,display=display.none)
int sweepLookbackBars=input.int(5,"Liquidity Sweep Lookback",minval=2,maxval=12,group=G2,display=display.none)

// Premium additions. All are additive quality evidence; none is a global hard filter.
bool useSessionDayLiquidity=input.bool(true,"Use Session / Previous-Day Sweep + Reclaim",group=G2,display=display.none)
string liquidityTimezone=input.string("Etc/UTC","Liquidity Session Timezone",group=G2,display=display.none)
string asiaSession=input.session("0000-0800","Asian Session",group=G2,display=display.none)
string londonSession=input.session("0800-1600","London Session",group=G2,display=display.none)
int sessionLevelMaxAgeHours=input.int(36,"Session Level Maximum Age (hours)",minval=8,maxval=72,group=G2,display=display.none)

bool useEmaRegime=input.bool(true,"Use EMA13 Slope + EMA50 Regime",group=G2,display=display.none)
const int regimeEmaLength=50
float emaSlopeMinATR=input.float(0.01,"Minimum EMA13 Slope / ATR",minval=0.0,maxval=0.20,step=0.005,group=G2,display=display.none)

bool useDisplacementChoch=input.bool(true,"Use Displacement-Quality CHoCH",group=G2,display=display.none)
float displacementMinRangeATR=input.float(0.70,"Displacement Minimum Range / ATR",minval=0.30,maxval=2.00,step=0.05,group=G2,display=display.none)
float displacementMinBodyPct=input.float(0.55,"Displacement Minimum Body %",minval=0.30,maxval=0.90,step=0.05,group=G2,display=display.none)
float displacementMinBreakATR=input.float(0.10,"Displacement Break Distance / ATR",minval=0.0,maxval=0.50,step=0.05,group=G2,display=display.none)

bool useVWAP=input.bool(true,"Use Daily VWAP Alignment / Reclaim",group=G2,display=display.none)
float vwapToleranceATR=input.float(0.20,"VWAP Tolerance / ATR",minval=0.05,maxval=0.75,step=0.05,group=G2,display=display.none)


float scalpStopPips=input.float(20.0,"Scalp SL Buffer",minval=10.0,maxval=150.0,step=5.0,group=G3,display=display.none)
float intradayStopPips=input.float(35.0,"Intraday SL Buffer",minval=10.0,maxval=300.0,step=5.0,group=G3,display=display.none)
float swingStopPips=input.float(70.0,"Swing SL Buffer",minval=20.0,maxval=600.0,step=10.0,group=G3,display=display.none)
